#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1810cacd-3565-5438-ae93-45b50970f5dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Trigonometric Ratio Given a Point on the Unit Circle"}] :question/id #uuid "ec8644e2-c365-5dce-bb21-7a148203a03a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10818" :question/problem "![](images/92/925a47f324868fb022b51ff490ccecc557e989054253ad643542a478deb094d7.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a unit circle. Given that the $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $-0.7,$ what is the value of $\\cos\\theta?$" :question/worked-solution "Any point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = \\sin\\theta\n$$\n\n![](images/f4/f438a90ea7afe511562058f49f13af29722aa137a8032a22ac16ca6566688cb7.png)\n\nWe're given that $x=-0.7$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = -0.7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b43c0b-f0bb-54eb-9644-6db9398ab0a9" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Sine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "ea7f4d67-8d88-559f-b39e-7618d86f9379" :question/math-academy-id "e-10819" :question/problem "What is $\\sin 335^\\circ$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "To express $\\sin{335^\\circ}$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta_R,$ we follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Find its reference angle $\\theta_R.$\n\n2\\. Calculate the value of the function for $\\theta_R.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle $335^\\circ$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/a7/a7456b0617c3c03ad55403e58904be26d826c90611c1a323553fa5c9f3149d66.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta = 335^\\circ$ is in the $4$th quadrant, the reference angle $\\theta_R$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & ={360}^{∘}-\\theta  \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{335}^{∘} \\\\  & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\sin{335^\\circ},$ and therefore we're interested in $\\sin\\theta_R = \\sin{25^\\circ}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\sin{335^\\circ}$ must be *negative* because the sine ratio is *always* negative in the $4$th quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin 335^\\circ = -\\sin{25^\\circ}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "669295c7-5c63-5926-907c-1e2c211c3570" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Cosine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "926813b0-e2fb-5671-8b99-a00c4710c4d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-10820" :question/problem "What is $\\cos 340^\\circ$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "To express $\\cos{340^\\circ}$ in terms of $\\cos\\theta_R,$ we follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Find its reference angle $\\theta_R.$\n\n2\\. Calculate the value of the function for $\\theta_R.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle $340^\\circ$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/c2/c263e4358de9cd29f1a97795e840d06cf4b198cf53c0630c2c12c85de7f00490.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta = 340^\\circ$ is in the $4$th quadrant, the reference angle $\\theta_R$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & ={360}^{∘}-\\theta  \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{340}^{∘} \\\\  & ={20}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\cos{340^\\circ},$ and therefore we're interested in $\\cos\\theta_R = \\cos{20^\\circ}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\cos{340^\\circ}$ must be *positive* because the cosine ratio is *always* positive in the $4$th quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\cos 340^\\circ = \\cos{20^\\circ}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81fb8ad6-b9b7-5d2b-9ea5-17c6df4dea68" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Tangent of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "0561b4af-2393-5bc1-99e0-9c996f13c4a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10822" :question/problem "What is $\\tan 162^\\circ$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "To express $\\tan{162^\\circ}$ in terms of $\\tan\\theta_R,$ we follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Find its reference angle $\\theta_R.$\n\n2\\. Calculate the value of the function for $\\theta_R.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle $162^\\circ$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/57/578c1aa397751d9cc6497e35443ff7b3508f3126f18c6650a26fbd4e74bde58e.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta = 162^\\circ$ is in the $2$nd quadrant, the reference angle $\\theta_R$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & ={180}^{∘}-\\theta  \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{162}^{∘} \\\\  & ={18}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\tan{162^\\circ}$, and therefore we're interested in $\\tan\\theta_R = \\tan{18^\\circ}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\tan{162^\\circ}$ must be *negative* because the tangent ratio is *always* negative in the $2$nd quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\tan 162^\\circ = -\\tan{18^\\circ}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b43c0b-f0bb-54eb-9644-6db9398ab0a9" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Sine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1025dd-8e11-5d31-93f4-a104a6891102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541484} {:answer/id #uuid "87b79138-3e5f-56f9-996f-a26677320370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{98}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541696} {:answer/id #uuid "d415a67b-c2a5-5629-8269-a52240a4b404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{98}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541871} {:answer/id #uuid "d428cd7c-998a-572e-8cec-28f6b2c5a90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541872} {:answer/id #uuid "d47d6158-6275-549c-b0c0-3244cf53d7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e1025dd-8e11-5d31-93f4-a104a6891102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541484} :answer-field/id #uuid "c04052dc-8f5a-5353-884d-cf6d75fec3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c9c8f3d-e984-5471-bc82-27a595032835" :question/math-academy-id "q-156073" :question/problem "What is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{262}^{∘}$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "To express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{262}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Find its reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}.$\n\n2\\. Calculate the value of the function for ${\\theta }_{R}.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle ${262}^{∘}$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/b6/b64a679dea08fe6472b146e0ae43cbfbc01577ef019619c3c44c6e22000c7c61.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta ={262}^{∘}$ is in the $3$rd quadrant, the reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\theta -{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={262}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={82}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{262}^{∘}$, and therefore we're interested in $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{262}^{∘}$ must be *negative* because the sine ratio is *always* negative in the $3$rd quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{262}^{∘}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "669295c7-5c63-5926-907c-1e2c211c3570" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Cosine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2013e8aa-4f6c-5cf8-86d1-fb6021658fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541488} {:answer/id #uuid "590fcb10-5fff-513d-ba1f-8b1ac85823c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541598} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3e4c0d-7d43-5e0a-8d3a-22094be279de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541810} {:answer/id #uuid "cac13f42-f2fe-540f-85c0-4dd91d075200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541851} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ad56e7-b175-54e7-bc99-0065661c5f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb3e4c0d-7d43-5e0a-8d3a-22094be279de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.t