alculate the value of the function for ${\\theta }_{R}.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle ${280}^{∘}$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/70/70c2ef3ed7982e487a23eb8332a3740d65800a9b3bac73b8209b2c3cdb9fa210.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta ={280}^{∘}$ is in the $4$th quadrant, the reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & ={360}^{∘}-\\theta  \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{280}^{∘} \\\\  & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{280}^{∘}$, and therefore we're interested in $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{80}^{∘}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{280}^{∘}$ must be *negative* because the tangent ratio is *always* negative in the $4$th quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{280}^{∘}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{80}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81fb8ad6-b9b7-5d2b-9ea5-17c6df4dea68" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Tangent of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09205301-c82f-54fc-9318-8476966aa8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{187}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541441} {:answer/id #uuid "4181b1d2-2fb7-5749-bf3d-257c6cfe7b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡{7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541558} {:answer/id #uuid "419395b4-36cd-5811-9644-53510deded67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡{97}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541560} {:answer/id #uuid "95e44251-8193-5969-9031-ac6f0fd94059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu